{
  "description": "Reviewed native Bloodpool marsh artwork. Source IDs are provenance only; runtime uses pixels, palette slots, collision and priority. Decks span the path, timber supports and shoreline rocks retain native water contact with shallow depth, and native water gains a continuous surface. Opaque infill follows supporting earth or shallow shoreline rock. NativePriorityScenery (1048576) keeps high-priority timber at the front while low-priority noncolliding timber stands behind the walking plane; colliding beam tops retain their deck geometry. PixelRecess (4194304) gives face_colors a distinct reviewed rear-mounted-ink meaning: only selected low-priority wood pixels in mixed water/post characters move to the post plane. Water ink and all high-priority artwork retain native placement; this is not a global palette-color rule.",
